# ai-sticker-generator

Starter repo for a pet meme / sticker generator. This repo is designed for a product where users upload pet photos and turn them into sticker-style animal meme images using a remote AI provider (e.g., Volcano / ByteDance Ark).

## Stack
- Vue 3 frontend
- FastAPI backend
- Celery + Redis worker
- MinIO object storage
- Docker Compose starter

## Local dev (demo / mock)

1. Start infra + backend

```bash
docker-compose up --build
```

2. Run frontend

```bash
cd frontend
npm install
npm run dev
```

Open http://localhost:5173

## Real AI provider config (Volcano / ByteDance)

Add the following env vars before starting the backend:

```bash
export MODEL_PROVIDER=volcano
export VOLCANO_API_URL=https://ark.cn-beijing.volces.com
export VOLCANO_API_KEY=your_key_here
export VOLCANO_MODEL=doubao-seed-1-6
```

Also supported:

```bash
export MODEL_API_URL=https://ark.cn-beijing.volces.com
export MODEL_API_KEY=your_key_here
```

The backend's provider abstraction is in `backend/app/model_client.py`.

## Why this is useful for your pet meme product

- Users upload their pet photo
- Optional: upload a reference meme or style image
- Backend sends the pet photo + reference style to the AI image generation service
- Result is stored in MinIO and returned as a downloadable sticker image

## Important notes
- If the provider API differs from the OpenAI-compatible shape, update the payload/response parsing in `backend/app/model_client.py`.
- Ensure your provider key is kept in environment variables or secrets, not committed to source control.
- Add user/content safety checks before publishing generated images.

## Project structure

- `backend/app` — FastAPI app + Celery worker + provider logic
- `frontend/src` — Vue UI
- `docker-compose.yml` — local infra
